# Disable pnpm 10's supply-chain minimum-release-age check.
#
# pnpm 10 enables a 24h release-age cutoff on every `install
# --frozen-lockfile`. For a starter kit whose dev deps are framework
# tools (wrangler, miniflare, secretlint, …) the policy creates a CI
# failure window any time a new dev-tool release lands, with no
# corresponding security benefit. Opt out here.
#
# Re-enable per-fork by setting `minimum-release-age=PT24H` (or any
# ISO-8601 duration) in your fork's `.npmrc`. The policy is meant for
# repos that ship to end users, not for short-lived dev-tool CI.
minimum-release-age=0
